<title>FRANCE: EU Parliament backs unchanged cereals set-aside.</title>
<headline>EU Parliament backs unchanged cereals set-aside.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament on Friday approved a proposal to keep the 1998 cereals compulsory set-aside rate at five percent.</p>
<p>EU farm ministers are now expected to approve the European Commission's proposal on Tuesday without discussion after unanimously calling last month for five percent.</p>
<p>An unchanged rate would help to maintain production and avoid rebuilding excessive stocks, the Commission said when it presented the proposal earlier this month.</p>
<p>Despite a record grain harvest last year due to exceptional yields, EU intervention stocks remained low due to a substantial increase in consumption and strong exports.</p>
</text>
